### =====================================================================
### appointMe - day15-working-hours.http   (Day 15: weekly working hours)
### SELF-CONTAINED: it logs in by itself and keeps its own tokens.
###
### BEFORE YOU START
###   1. Put the NEW scripts/dev-seed.sql in place (it now also seeds working hours).
###   2. Start the app once so Flyway applies V3__working_hours.sql.
###   3. Reload the seed:
###        Get-Content .\scripts\dev-seed.sql | docker exec -i appointme-db psql -U appointme -d appointme
###
### Cast (password for all: correct-horse-1)
###   ALICE = OWNER of tenant 1, membership 1
###   BOB   = STAFF in tenant 1, membership 2   (the staff member we edit most)
###   GUS   = OWNER of tenant 2, membership 4
###   Membership 3 = Bob in tenant 2 (foreign to Alice)
###
### The {staffId} in the URL is a MEMBERSHIP id (same number you use as staffId
### when booking an appointment).
###
### Seed data: Alice Mon-Fri 09:00-17:00 | Bob Mon-Fri 09:00-13:00 + 14:00-18:00
###            Gus Mon-Fri 08:00-16:00
### Days are names: MONDAY ... SUNDAY. Times are "HH:mm" (24 hour clock).
### Run top to bottom: later requests depend on the data earlier ones leave.
### Tokens last 30 minutes. Sudden 401s => rerun SETUP.
### =====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080


### ======================================================================
### SETUP
### ======================================================================

### A1. Alice logs in. EXPECT 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@test.com", "password": "correct-horse-1" }

> {%
    client.global.set("aliceUserToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### A2. Alice selects tenant 1. EXPECT 200, OWNER
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/select-tenant/1
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceUserToken}}

> {%
    client.global.set("aliceToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### B1. Bob logs in. EXPECT 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "bob@test.com", "password": "correct-horse-1" }

> {%
    client.global.set("bobUserToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### B2. Bob selects tenant 1. EXPECT 200, STAFF
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/select-tenant/1
Authorization: Bearer {{bobUserToken}}

> {%
    client.global.set("bobToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### G1. Gus logs in. EXPECT 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "gus@test.com", "password": "correct-horse-1" }

> {%
    client.global.set("gusUserToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### G2. Gus selects tenant 2. EXPECT 200, OWNER
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/select-tenant/2
Authorization: Bearer {{gusUserToken}}

> {%
    client.global.set("gusToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}


### ======================================================================
### 1. READ the seeded schedules (owner)
### ======================================================================

### H1. Bob's schedule. EXPECT 200, staffId 2, 10 intervals:
###     Mon-Fri 09:00-13:00 and 14:00-18:00, sorted by day, then start time
GET {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### H2. Alice's own schedule. EXPECT 200, staffId 1, 5 intervals (Mon-Fri 09:00-17:00)
GET {{baseUrl}}/staff/1/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}


### ======================================================================
### 2. REPLACE a schedule (PUT replaces the WHOLE week)
### ======================================================================

### H3. New schedule for Bob. EXPECT 200, exactly 3 intervals:
###     MONDAY 10:00-18:00, TUESDAY 10:00-14:00, TUESDAY 15:00-19:00
PUT {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "intervals": [
    { "dayOfWeek": "TUESDAY", "start": "15:00", "end": "19:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "MONDAY",  "start": "10:00", "end": "18:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "TUESDAY", "start": "10:00", "end": "14:00" }
  ]
}

### H4. Read it back. EXPECT 200, the same 3 intervals (sorted) and NONE of the old 10
GET {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### H5. Back-to-back intervals touch but do not overlap. EXPECT 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "intervals": [
    { "dayOfWeek": "WEDNESDAY", "start": "09:00", "end": "13:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "WEDNESDAY", "start": "13:00", "end": "17:00" }
  ]
}

### H6. The same clock times on DIFFERENT days are fine. EXPECT 200, 3 intervals
PUT {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "intervals": [
    { "dayOfWeek": "MONDAY",    "start": "09:00", "end": "17:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "WEDNESDAY", "start": "09:00", "end": "17:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "FRIDAY",    "start": "09:00", "end": "17:00" }
  ]
}

### H7. Empty list = no working hours at all (a week off). EXPECT 200, "intervals": []
PUT {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "intervals": [] }

### H8. Read it back. EXPECT 200, "intervals": []
GET {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### H9. Restore Bob's normal week (needed by the tests below). EXPECT 200, 10 intervals
PUT {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "intervals": [
    { "dayOfWeek": "MONDAY",    "start": "09:00", "end": "13:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "MONDAY",    "start": "14:00", "end": "18:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "TUESDAY",   "start": "09:00", "end": "13:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "TUESDAY",   "start": "14:00", "end": "18:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "WEDNESDAY", "start": "09:00", "end": "13:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "WEDNESDAY", "start": "14:00", "end": "18:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "THURSDAY",  "start": "09:00", "end": "13:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "THURSDAY",  "start": "14:00", "end": "18:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "FRIDAY",    "start": "09:00", "end": "13:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "FRIDAY",    "start": "14:00", "end": "18:00" }
  ]
}


### ======================================================================
### 3. VALIDATION   (all EXPECT 400; Bob's saved schedule must NOT change)
### ======================================================================

### V1. End before start. EXPECT 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "intervals": [ { "dayOfWeek": "MONDAY", "start": "17:00", "end": "09:00" } ] }

### V2. End equals start (an empty interval). EXPECT 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "intervals": [ { "dayOfWeek": "MONDAY", "start": "09:00", "end": "09:00" } ] }

### V3. Overlap on the same day (12:00 is inside 09:00-13:00). EXPECT 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "intervals": [
    { "dayOfWeek": "MONDAY", "start": "09:00", "end": "13:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "MONDAY", "start": "12:00", "end": "15:00" }
  ]
}

### V4. The exact same interval twice. EXPECT 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "intervals": [
    { "dayOfWeek": "MONDAY", "start": "09:00", "end": "13:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "MONDAY", "start": "09:00", "end": "13:00" }
  ]
}

### V5. One interval fully inside another, listed out of order. EXPECT 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "intervals": [
    { "dayOfWeek": "THURSDAY", "start": "10:00", "end": "11:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "THURSDAY", "start": "09:00", "end": "17:00" }
  ]
}

### V6. Atomic replace: after ALL the failures above, Bob must still have the 10 intervals
###     from H9. EXPECT 200, 10 intervals. (A failed PUT must change nothing.)
GET {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### V7. Not a day name. EXPECT 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "intervals": [ { "dayOfWeek": "FUNDAY", "start": "09:00", "end": "17:00" } ] }

### V8. Field "intervals" missing. EXPECT 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ }

### V9. "intervals": null. EXPECT 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "intervals": null }

### V10. An interval without "start". EXPECT 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "intervals": [ { "dayOfWeek": "MONDAY", "end": "17:00" } ] }

### V11. A time that does not exist. EXPECT 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "intervals": [ { "dayOfWeek": "MONDAY", "start": "25:00", "end": "26:00" } ] }

### V12. A null inside the list. EXPECT 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "intervals": [ null ] }

### V13. Too many intervals (limit is 50; 51 here). EXPECT 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/staff/2/working-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "intervals": [
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"00:00","end":"00:10"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"00:20","end":"00:30"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"00:40","end":"00:50"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"01:00","end":"01:10"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"01:20","end":"01:30"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"01:40","end":"01:50"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"02:00","end":"02:10"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"02:20","end":"02:30"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"02:40","end":"02:50"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"03:00","end":"03:10"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"03:20","end":"03:30"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"03:40","end":"03:50"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"04:00","end":"04:10"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"04:20","end":"04:30"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"04:40","end":"04:50"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"05:00","end":"05:10"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"05:20","end":"05:30"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"05:40","end":"05:50"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"06:00","end":"06:10"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"06:20","end":"06:30"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"06:40","end":"06:50"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"07:00","end":"07:10"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"07:20","end":"07:30"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"07:40","end":"07:50"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"08:00","end":"08:10"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"08:20","end":"08:30"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"08:40","end":"08:50"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"09:00","end":"09:10"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"09:20","end":"09:30"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"09:40","end":"09:50"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"10:00","end":"10:10"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"10:20","end":"10:30"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"10:40","end":"10:50"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"11:00","end":"11:10"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"11:20","end":"11:30"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"11:40","end":"11:50"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"12:00","end":"12:10"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"12:20","end":"12:30"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"12:40","end":"12:50"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"13:00","end":"13:10"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"13:20","end":"13:30"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"13:40","end":"13:50"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"14:00","end":"14:10"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"14:20","end":"14:30"},
    {"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"14:40","end":"14:50"},{"dayOfWeek":"MONDAY","start":"15:00","end":"15:10"},
